// Pull request: #6638 New Rule: Uncommon Child Process Of WFMFormat.EXE
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6638
// Pull request author: COMPUMAX-EC
// Change: new rule
// Title: Uncommon Child Process Of WFMFormat.EXE
// Sigma ID: ece66131-245f-4dcc-a630-f3bdf79a4e7a
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Geovanny Basantes
// Date: 2026-11-06 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects uncommon child processes of WFMFormat.EXE, a command-line tool shipped with the
//   Microsoft Message Farm Analyzer used to pretty-print dump files. WFMFormat.EXE executes
//   "tracerpt.exe" from its own folder, which allows attackers to drop an arbitrary binary named
//   "tracerpt.exe" next to it and proxy its execution through a Microsoft signed binary.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/WFMFormat/
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=103244
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/d7dce9f1289defddb3e8c26be0342331a4739d74/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wfmformat_uncommon_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\WFMFormat.exe" and (not(((FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\System32\\tracerpt.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\tracerpt.exe") or (FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\System32\\conhost.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\System32\\WerFault.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\WerFault.exe"))))
